Give bottom-half callbacks the prototype they are called with

ELinks queues deferred work as "bottom halves". The event loop calls every
queued function as select_handler_T, that is `void (*)(void *)`:

    typedef void (*select_handler_T)(void *);
    #define register_bottom_half(fn, data) \
            register_bottom_half_do((select_handler_T) (fn), (void *) (data))

Two callers register a function that takes no argument and rely on that
cast to hide the difference:

    check_queue(void)       src/network/connection.c
    update_status(void)     src/js/quickjs/unibar.c

Calling a function through a pointer to an incompatible function type is
undefined behavior (C11 6.3.2.3p8). Native calling conventions happen to
tolerate an extra argument, but a WebAssembly indirect call checks the
callee's signature and traps: every page load queues check_queue, so
ELinks died with "null function or function signature mismatch" before
rendering anything. The same code fails under control-flow-integrity
checking (clang -fsanitize=cfi-icall) on native targets.

Fix both registrations so the queued function really has the handler
prototype. check_queue is static and only ever called as a bottom half,
so it simply gains the unused parameter; update_status has direct callers,
so it gets a small adapter.

This is a portability fix, not a Kandelo adaptation: nothing here is
specific to one platform.

--- a/src/js/quickjs/unibar.c
+++ b/src/js/quickjs/unibar.c
@@ -57,6 +57,15 @@
 #undef unibar_fetch
 }
 
+/* update_status() takes no argument, but a bottom half is called with one
+ * pointer argument, so register a function of the matching type. */
+static void
+update_status_bottom_half(void *data_)
+{
+	ELOG
+	update_status();
+}
+
 static JSValue
 js_unibar_set_property_visible(JSContext *ctx, JSValueConst this_val, JSValue val, int magic)
 {
@@ -87,7 +96,7 @@
 	default:
 		break;
 	}
-	register_bottom_half(update_status, NULL);
+	register_bottom_half(update_status_bottom_half, NULL);
 
 	return JS_UNDEFINED;
 }
--- a/src/network/connection.c
+++ b/src/network/connection.c
@@ -881,8 +881,10 @@
 	return 1;
 }
 
+/* Registered as a bottom half, so it must have select_handler_T's
+ * prototype: the event loop calls it with one pointer argument. */
 static void
-check_queue(void)
+check_queue(void *data_)
 {
 	ELOG
 	struct connection *conn;
